<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Preview My Post" description="Learn how Preview My Post handles browser-based image processing, local settings, analytics events, and contact information.">
	<article class="legal-page"><span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="lead">The tool is designed so your creative stays under your control.</p>
	<h2>Image Processing</h2><p>Images selected for the preview workspace are processed locally in your browser whenever practical using temporary browser object URLs. Preview My Post does not intentionally upload your image to its server. Uploaded image data is not stored in local storage unless a future feature clearly asks for your explicit choice.</p>
	<h2>Local Storage</h2><p>Non-sensitive settings—such as website theme, preview appearance, active mode, safe-zone preferences, and optional draft preview fields—may be stored locally on your device. You can remove them by resetting the tool or clearing site data in your browser.</p>
	<h2>Analytics</h2><p>The site may record privacy-conscious product events such as image uploaded, example loaded, tab selected, safe zones enabled, issue viewed, caption added, image replaced, tool reset, return visit, and landing page used. Events must not contain uploaded image content or personal caption text.</p>
	<h2>Advertising & Third Parties</h2><p>Reserved areas may support advertising later. Advertising or measurement partners may use their own cookies or similar technologies only when configured and disclosed. The core tool remains usable without interacting with an ad.</p>
	<h2>Contact</h2><p>Questions about this policy can be sent through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p></article>
</Layout>
